define-github-release-query-interface

Lane: cross

Unit: monitor-codex-releases-through-github

ChildPatch: define-github-release-query-interface

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema

Purpose: Query and monitor Codex releases independently of Telegram while exposing current GitHub observations to app-server clients and notification subscribers.

Requires: Unit:cross/configure-integrations-through-shared-file, Unit:cross/configure-application-proxy-at-runtime

Provides: Read GitHub settings from the shared integrations document, query the ten newest release records through the shared HTTP routing owner, select stable and prerelease channels independently, retain successful-check time and remaining GraphQL points, publish nonblocking cached github/read and throttled github/check interfaces, and provide process-scoped observation subscriptions.

Boundary: GitHub owns network queries, current observations and check scheduling without requiring Telegram credentials or delivery. Failed checks clear current observations. Notification consumers own silent initial baselines, selection and successful delivery tracking. Preserve private credentials, bounded response bodies, disabled redirects and request logging, configured cadence, manual throttling and cancellation. No legacy Telegram configuration reader or credential-setting UI is introduced.

Verification: Focused protocol and app-server tests verify independent cached reads, stable and prerelease selection, field-selected bounded queries, redacted errors, failed-check clearing, manual throttling, shared observation subscriptions and worker shutdown without contacting real services.

CrossGroup: control-center


